WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.190
(gentle percussion music)

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:04.980
- It's no secret that,
on a day-to-day basis,

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:07.830
most people claim to lack
the motivation necessary

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:11.220
to make any significant
positive changes in their lives.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:12.920
It's almost a meme in today's culture

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:15.930
that people are just generally
lazy and unmotivated,

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:18.810
helpless against their own
primal desires to veg out

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:21.580
and scroll Instagram,
cringing at the very thought

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:24.150
of dropping the phone and
cleaning their entire kitchen.

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.740
Every once in a while,
though, something triggers us.

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:30.280
Maybe it's a deadline, a
post we saw on Instagram,

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:33.100
or a Tony Robbins video we
just happened to stumble across

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:36.570
on YouTube, and it gives us
the adequate inspiration needed

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:38.400
to perform the actions necessary

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.150
for improving our situation.

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:43.090
But here's something
that almost nobody knows.

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:46.020
Action is not just the
effect of motivation,

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:47.930
but also the cause of it.

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:49.940
Most people only commit to action,

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:52.120
when they feel motivated to do so.

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:53.550
And they only feel motivated

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:56.540
when they feel a certain amount
of emotional inspiration.

00:00:56.540 --> 00:01:00.120
Emotional inspiration gives
us the adequate motivation

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.090
to perform a constructive action.

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:04.370
But there's a huge
problem with this system.

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:06.570
Aside from the issue
that inspiration seems

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:08.770
to strike us randomly and unpredictably,

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:10.470
there's an even bigger problem.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.890
Often, our negative attitudes
towards our bad situations

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:16.100
hinders us from experiencing any sort

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:19.040
of emotional inspiration
towards changing the situation

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:20.210
in the first place.

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:22.940
If you have an attitude
of massive guilt, shame,

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:26.080
resentment or fear towards
your current situation,

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:28.200
then the very thought of
confronting this monster

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:30.230
is likely to inspire the very emotions

00:01:30.230 --> 00:01:32.600
that put you in that
situation to begin with.

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:34.090
It's a Catch-22.

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:35.450
So how do you fix this?

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:38.920
Well, by realizing that
emotional inspiration,

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:41.930
adequate motivation,
to constructive action

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:43.740
is not a linear sequence,

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:45.090
it's an endless loop.

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:47.310
And you can start wherever
you want to start.

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:50.620
Inspiration leads to motivation,
which leads to action,

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:51.960
which leads to inspiration,

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:54.310
which leads to motivation, et cetera.

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:56.370
If you lack the inspiration or motivation

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:59.430
to take constructive
action, then do something.

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:00.530
Anything really.

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:02.770
Then harness the reaction from that action

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:04.690
to give you the adequate inspiration

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:06.770
and motivation to take further action.

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:07.603
And you might be thinking,

00:02:07.603 --> 00:02:09.640
"Well, how am I supposed to do something

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:11.260
without any inspiration?"

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:13.480
Well, whether you realize it or not,

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:15.150
you do this all the time.

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:16.830
Ever notice you're much more productive

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:19.210
after taking a shower and getting dressed?

00:02:19.210 --> 00:02:20.870
Did you have to have some sort of big,

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:23.830
inspirational epiphany in
order to take a shower?

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:25.503
No, it's just something you do.

00:02:25.503 --> 00:02:27.230
(shower splashing)
Some actions require little

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:29.410
to no inspiration whatsoever,
(toothbrush cleaning)

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:30.820
and those are the very actions
(spray spritzing)

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:32.420
whose reactions you should harness

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:33.990
into taking further action.

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:37.150
So next time you're avoiding
some huge thing you gotta do,

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:39.820
don't just sit there and
wait for inspiration to hit.

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:41.300
Just go and do something.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:43.580
Then harness the reaction from that action

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:45.420
to give you the adequate inspiration

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:47.780
and motivation to take further action.

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:50.590
And this is the Do Something Principle.

